From 2c2df658a5575060816e3e970699f87c332119ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:43:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 331/345] wifi: mt76: take the remaining wcids off the phy
 tx_list at reset

mt76_reset_device() runs INIT_LIST_HEAD() on each phy->tx_list while
wcids that are not in dev->wcid[] can still be on it, such as a station
between .sta_pre_rcu_remove and its removal. The later
mt76_wcid_cleanup() of such a wcid then corrupts the list.

Take the remaining wcids off the list under the tx_lock.

Fixes: 065c79df595a ("wifi: mt76: mt7915: fix list corruption after hardware restart")
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261119124352.1842164-3-nbd@nbd.name
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
[replace phy->dev->tx_lock with phy->tx_lock]
(cherry picked from commit 2c2df658a5575060816e3e970699f87c332119ec)
---
 mac80211.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mac80211.c b/mac80211.c
index adeb8de5..4378d285 100644
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -829,7 +829,11 @@ static void mt76_reset_phy(struct mt76_phy *phy)
 	if (!phy)
 		return;
 
-	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&phy->tx_list);
+	spin_lock_bh(&phy->tx_lock);
+	while (!list_empty(&phy->tx_list))
+		list_del_init(phy->tx_list.next);
+	spin_unlock_bh(&phy->tx_lock);
+
 	phy->num_sta = 0;
 	phy->chanctx = NULL;
 	mt76_roc_complete(phy);
